Description: terminal VM manager for QEMU without libvirt
 kudu creates and manages QEMU virtual machines from a terminal
 interface, as an alternative to virt-manager or GNOME Boxes. It
 talks to QEMU directly over QMP rather than through libvirt, and
 uses cloud-init images for guest provisioning.
 .
 KVM acceleration is used where /dev/kvm is available and the
 interface reports its absence rather than refusing to start.
